=== per-block interrupt-poll cost, in a translated loop (guest EL1) ===
  CNTFRQ_EL0 = 24000000 Hz

  Each section retires exactly 2,000,000 translated x86 instructions
  (1 x86 insn = 4 ARM ops; 40% memory-touching; 8 chained blocks/iteration)

  x86/blk       none    ld+cbnz   hdr-only   cbnz-reg    ld/blk%     hdr% reg/blk%
  5            499us       498us       500us       497us     -0.24%   +0.07%   -0.58%
  10           499us       497us       499us       497us     -0.32%   +0.00%   -0.32%
  20           498us       497us       503us       498us     -0.17%   +0.97%   -0.08%
  40           498us       498us       502us       497us     +0.01%   +0.96%   -0.15%
  80           499us       498us       499us       498us     -0.11%   +0.12%   -0.09%

  per-x86-instruction cost, and per-check cost in ns:
  x86/blk ns/x86insn  ns/ld-check ns/reg-check
  5           0.250       -0.003       -0.007
  10          0.249       -0.008       -0.008
  20          0.249       -0.008       -0.004
  40          0.249        0.001       -0.015
  80          0.249       -0.022       -0.018

  drift control (same section run twice, k=5 and k=80):
    k=5  none 499us / 507us   ld+cbnz 498us / 498us  (-0.24% vs -1.72%)
    k=80 none 499us / 498us   ld+cbnz 498us / 499us  (-0.11% vs +0.26%)

  check-density slope: n checks inside every 5-x86-instruction block
  (400,000 blocks per section; slope = marginal ns per check)
  n/block    ld+cbnz us     ns/check    cbnz-reg us     ns/check
  0                 499       0.0000              -            -
  1                 498      -0.0046            506       0.0166
  2                 500       0.0004            499      -0.0009
  4                 516       0.0103            519       0.0124
  8                 600       0.0315            611       0.0347
  16                964       0.0725            965       0.0728
  32               1917       0.1107           1919       0.1109
  baseline (n=0) measured twice: 499 us / 500 us  (drift +0.08%)

=== translated REP MOVSQ: how do you keep it interruptible? ===
  4096 elements x 512 repeats = 2,097,152 8-byte element copies per section
  strategy                            total    ns/elem   overhead worst-case IRQ
  no check (uninterruptible)          636us      0.303      +0.0%      unbounded
  load+cbnz every element             692us      0.330      +8.9%          0.3 ns
  load+cbnz every 8                   861us      0.410     +35.3%          3.3 ns
  load+cbnz every 64                  651us      0.311      +2.5%         19.9 ns
  load+cbnz every 512                 699us      0.333      +9.9%        170.6 ns
  cbnz reg every element              635us      0.303      -0.2%          0.3 ns
  no check (repeat)                   628us      0.300      -1.2%      unbounded

=== EL1 code-cache self-patch and timer-arm costs ===
  bare STR to the code page                          0.76 ns
  STR + DC CVAU + DSB ISH + IC IVAU + DSB + ISB    110.77 ns
  ISB alone                                          8.93 ns
  MRS CNTVCT_EL0                                     0.54 ns
  arm a deadline (MRS CNTVCT + MSR CVAL + CTL)       4.76 ns

  host exits during the whole run: 1
